1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,140
Listen to a talk in a music class.

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:07,100
You are probably all familiar with jazz music.

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:10,140
Its history begins in the southern United States.

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:14,680
It originated in the early 20th century in the city of New Orleans,

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:19,220
blending elements of different kinds of music like African rhythms, blues, and ragtime.

6
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:24,150
One of the key characteristics of jazz is its emphasis on improvisation.

7
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:27,340
Musicians often create spontaneous melodies

8
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:30,140
and harmonies, making each performance unique.

9
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:32,680
This contrasts with classical music

10
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:35,240
where compositions are typically played as written.

11
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,335
Jazz musicians also use syncopation,

12
00:00:37,335 --> 00:00:44,040
which involves shifting the normal accents in the rhythm to create an unexpected and exciting sound.

13
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:47,200
In the 1920s, jazz became widely popular

14
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:50,180
and moved north to cities like Chicago and New York City.

15
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:53,784
During the Jazz Age, as this period became known,

16
00:00:53,784 --> 00:00:57,760
famous jazz musicians like Louis Armstrong became household names

17
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:00,190
and jazz clubs flourished as social hubs.

18
00:01:00,190 --> 00:01:02,636
Over time, jazz continued to evolve,

19
00:01:02,636 --> 00:01:07,120
in part by incorporating elements from other musical traditions and cultures.

20
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:10,120
Today, it remains a vibrant and influential genre

21
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,090
celebrated for its creativity and expressive power.

22
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:17,260
Next, we will look at the impact of jazz on other musical genres

23
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,830
and how it has shaped contemporary music.
